  "format": "build",
  "skills": [
    "logic.decoder"
  ],
  "brief": {
    "story": "The rack has four relays and a two-bit address (A, B): exactly one relay should be on for each address, 00 to 11. That’s a 2-to-4 decoder: two inverters (IC1) and four ANDs (IC2). Output Y2 (B on, A off) isn’t wired.",
    "goal": "Wire IC2’s gate 3 so Y2 lights only for B = 1, A = 0, and each address lights exactly one LED.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "2-to-4 decoder",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Y0",
          "NOT A · NOT B"
        ],
        [
          "Y1",
          "A · NOT B"
        ],
        [
          "Y2",
          "NOT A · B (gate 3: pins 9, 10)"
        ],
        [
          "Y3",
          "A · B"
        ],
        [
          "NOT A",
          "column 4"
        ],
        [
          "B",
          "column 5"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "Each output is the AND of the inputs, each in its true or inverted form. Y2 = NOT A AND B.",
    "Gate 3’s inputs are pin 9 (column 22, bottom) and pin 10 (column 21, bottom). NOT A is on column 4 (IC1 pin 2), B on column 5.",
    "Column 4 → column 22 bottom, and column 5 → column 21 bottom."
  ],
