  "debrief": "A decoder turns a binary number into “one line out of many”: 2 bits pick 1 of 4, 3 bits 1 of 8 (the 74HC138). That’s how a computer’s address bus selects one memory chip out of several, and how a microcontroller drives many LEDs or relays from a few pins."
